# project-gitignore/2 — the mesh minimum a project must ignore (ptah). Keep this line:
# a copy without a version is a silent fork the moment it is made. `ptah verify <root>`
# MEASURES every rule below with `git check-ignore`, so wording is yours to change and
# the effect is not. Re-take the current block with: ptah gitignore-block

# Session-generated utilities cache
tools/scratch/

# Obsidian vault — the vault CONFIG is tracked ON PURPOSE: the project root IS
# the vault, so a fresh clone must open as a working vault (userIgnoreFilters
# included). Only machine-specific workspace state is ignored. Ignoring
# .obsidian/ wholesale means a clone of this project is NOT a vault, and nothing
# fails locally to tell you — see bbs n-271 / n-273.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/workspaces.json
.obsidian/cache/
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json
.trash/

# Secrets — never commit credentials
*.key
*apikey*
.env

# THE AUTHOR'S OPT-OUT — the git twin of Nextcloud's *.nxl (c-011/operator, n-822).
# Name a file *.gtxcl (or *.gtxcl.<anything>) to DECLARE that it must never be
# stored in git, instead of leaving a sweeper to INFER it from a directory name.
# It lives HERE and not in ~/.config/git/ignore because a global ignore does not
# travel with a clone: the marker is only worth using if every clone honours it.
# ⚠️ IT ONLY WORKS BEFORE THE FIRST COMMIT. Renaming an ALREADY-TRACKED file to
# *.gtxcl does NOT untrack it — `git add -A` keeps committing it and the old name's
# content stays in the history for ever (measured, ptah/1.22). To retire a tracked
# file: `git rm --cached <f>` first, and treat anything already committed as public.
# `ptah verify` FAILS on a tracked *.gtxcl, because that file says "never store me"
# while being stored.
# ⇒ *.nxl is the same in this respect — measured by c-001 (n-827): adding a pattern
# unsyncs nothing that is already on the server. NEITHER MARKER RETRACTS, and that is
# a decision rather than a limitation: a marker that retracts is a marker that DELETES,
# and where the server holds the only copy the retraction destroys the thing instead of
# unpublishing it. Both markers declare BEFORE the first commit/sync; cleaning up after
# stays a manual act, on purpose.
*.gtxcl
*.gtxcl.*

# Contacts.md is LOCAL ONLY: this repository is public and the file may hold
# contacts that are not. It stays at the project root, untracked.
Contacts.md
